+    // reconstruct graph based on new edge info.
+    // [TRS PATCH 2026-10-19] Graph.fromEdges only materializes vertices that touch
+    // an inter-community edge. A community fully internalized in step1 has no such
+    // edge, so it vanished from the compressed graph and its vertices were silently
+    // dropped from the final Louvain result (isolated small connected components
+    // output 0 rows). Emit every community as a 0-weight self-loop so all super
+    // vertices exist in the compressed graph:
+    //   - 0-weight keeps degree/modularity bookkeeping unchanged: the self-loop adds
+    //     0.0 to the super vertex degree in createLouvainGraph, contributes 0.0 to
+    //     k_i,n in getNeighCommInfo, and next round's step2 filters it into v2vKin
+    //     with weight*2 = 0 (no double counting with k_i,n);
+    //   - it also guarantees every vertex has a triplet, keeping the inner join in
+    //     getChangeInfo complete for isolated super vertices.
+    val selfLoops   = superVertexInfo.map(x => Edge(x._1, x._1, 0.0))
+    val initG        = Graph.fromEdges(edges.union(selfLoops), None)
     var louvainGraph = LouvainGraphUtil.createLouvainGraph(initG)
